{#-
  /run/proximos/portal/config.yaml — read by portal/src/config.rs (RUNTIME_CONFIG_PATH).

  BYTE-COMPATIBLE WITH proximos-render.sh's OUTPUT, deliberately. Everything below the
  header comment is the same nine keys in the same order with the same quoting, because
  the shell shim is what shipped and the Rust renderer replacing it must be provably a
  no-op before the shim can be deleted (WP-G removes it "only after WP-C parity").
  crates/proximos-render/tests/shim_parity.rs carries that shim's exact output as a
  fixture and diffs body-for-body against this template's.

  The header comment itself is the one intentional difference: it names the renderer that
  wrote the file, and that is no longer a shell script.

  The optional keys at the bottom are emitted only when an overlay sets them. The
  shim got that behaviour by appending the whole override file after the block above and
  relying on serde_yaml's last-key-wins — which, as its own header admitted, is a
  property of one vendored parser version rather than anything YAML guarantees. Here the
  keys are merged before rendering, so the emitted document has each key exactly once.

  `thresholds` (plan/portal/threshold_defaults.md §2) is set by defaults.yaml, so unlike
  the keys above it renders on every Hub; it is a post-shim key in shim_parity.rs.

  The last five are whole SECTIONS (devices.backend.md §3 WP0.3, `thresholds`, and
  calibration.cs.md §3's `calibration`),
  emitted through `| tojson` as a YAML flow mapping on one line. That is not a shortcut around block
  style: YAML is a superset of JSON, so the portal's serde_yaml reads the flow form into
  the same struct, and emitting it this way means the indentation of a nested section is
  not something a Jinja template has to get right for an arbitrary depth of operator
  input. Same reason `cookie_secure` uses the filter -- render what the format actually
  specifies, do not hand-format it.
-#}
# Rendered by `proximosctl render` (crates/proximos-render). Regenerated on
# every boot; edits made directly to this file are lost on the next render.
# Put per-device overrides in /data/proximos/config/proximos.config.yaml
# (its `portal:` section) or /data/portal/config.yaml instead.
bind_addr: "{{ portal.bind_addr }}"
mqtt_host: "{{ portal.mqtt_host }}"
mqtt_port: {{ portal.mqtt_port }}
topic_prefix: "{{ portal.topic_prefix }}"
mqtt_client_id: "{{ portal.mqtt_client_id }}"
data_dir: "{{ portal.data_dir }}"
templates_dir: "{{ portal.templates_dir }}"
static_dir: "{{ portal.static_dir }}"
db_key: "{{ db_key }}"
cookie_secure: {{ portal.cookie_secure | tojson }}
maintenance_window:
  start_utc: "{{ portal.maintenance_window.start_utc }}"
  duration_minutes: {{ portal.maintenance_window.duration_minutes }}
{% if portal.mqtt_username is not none %}
mqtt_username: "{{ portal.mqtt_username }}"
{% endif %}
{% if portal.mqtt_password is not none %}
mqtt_password: "{{ portal.mqtt_password }}"
{% endif %}
{% if portal.experimental_features_enabled is not none %}
experimental_features_enabled: {{ portal.experimental_features_enabled | tojson }}
{% endif %}
{% if portal.nodes is not none %}
nodes: {{ portal.nodes | tojson }}
{% endif %}
{% if portal.beacons is not none %}
beacons: {{ portal.beacons | tojson }}
{% endif %}
{% if portal.signal_quality is not none %}
signal_quality: {{ portal.signal_quality | tojson }}
{% endif %}
{% if portal.thresholds is not none %}
thresholds: {{ portal.thresholds | tojson }}
{% endif %}
{% if portal.calibration is not none %}
calibration: {{ portal.calibration | tojson }}
{% endif %}
